Experimenting with the interplay between different stages of image processing and conversion, 
\f2\i Anti_Shadow
\f1\i0 , serves as a catalyst for metaphysical transformations. The acrylic reproduction of the shadow photograph not only materialises the shadow but also reverses its reaction to light. The lights and floating acrylic bed turn the space into a sterile science fiction laboratory, a place for exercising experiments and playing with the foundational structure of light. Through the image processing, colour data is used to act in place as \'91height information\'92 to reveal underlying forms in the image. }